# Canonical MinaGuard verification-key hashes, one per network.
#
# NETWORK_DOMAIN is baked into the circuit as a compile-time constant
# (Field(1) for mainnet, Field(2) for testnet and devnet), so mainnet and the
# test-network aliases have distinct VKs. Verify that the deployed account has
# the VK for its actual network; the circuit cannot detect a misdeployment.
#
# Backend deployments: set MINAGUARD_VK_HASH to the hash for your target
# network (testnet hash for a testnet backend, mainnet hash for mainnet).
#
# Regenerate after any change under contracts/src:
#   MINA_NETWORK_DOMAIN=testnet bun run dev-helpers/cli.ts vk-hash compile
#   MINA_NETWORK_DOMAIN=mainnet bun run dev-helpers/cli.ts vk-hash compile
#   MINA_NETWORK_DOMAIN=devnet bun run dev-helpers/cli.ts vk-hash compile
# Then update all three lines below with the printed hashes.
testnet=5315622915005419723568327835818579142303669325041889347008595126408976471257
mainnet=27145310688905115202160621558038794741033440662094409814938833958313199151913
devnet=5315622915005419723568327835818579142303669325041889347008595126408976471257
